 "applies_to": "Seneca Z-10-D-IN hardware 2 with the 32-bit counter firmware, per user manual MI00253-10-EN.",
 "summary": "The Z-10-D-IN reads ten digital inputs and counts pulses on each, with counters kept in non-volatile FeRAM. Over RS-485 Modbus RTU it exposes input states, 16- and 32-bit counters, and per-input period, frequency and high time.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
